<Base title="Our Stay — Breanna & Eric">
  <PageTitle title="Our Stay" />
  <Section align="center">
    <p>We’ve reserved Borgo Laticastelli for the weekend, and we’re planning for our guests to stay with us at the borgo from Thursday through Sunday. Having everyone together in one place is one of the things we’re most excited about.</p>
  </Section>
  <Figure bleed ratio="21 / 9" label="Venue photo: terrace dining at sunset" />

  <Section>
    <h2>Your Stay</h2>
    <p>Guests staying at Laticastelli should plan to arrive on Thursday, September 16 and check out on Sunday, September 19. Check-in begins at 3:00 PM on Thursday, and checkout is by 12:00 PM on Sunday.</p>
    <p>You will not need to reserve a room directly with the hotel. Our wedding planner, Ani, will be helping us coordinate room assignments and stay details for the weekend, and personalized lodging information will be shared with each household.</p>
    <p><em>Your household’s lodging details and RSVP information will be shared privately through Joy.</em></p>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <h2>What’s Included</h2>
    <p>Breakfast is included each morning of your stay, and guests will have access to the borgo’s pool and shared spaces throughout the weekend.</p>
    <p>Rooms and suites include modern comforts such as air conditioning, Wi-Fi, private bathrooms, hair dryers, safes, and in-room refreshment facilities.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section tight>
    <Figure ratio="3 / 2" label="Venue photo: aerial pool" />
    <Figure narrow ratio="2 / 3" label="Venue photo: stone doorway" />
    <Figure ratio="3 / 2" label="Venue photo: bedroom" />
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <h2>Life at the Borgo</h2>
    <p>Laticastelli is tucked into the Tuscan countryside, but the weekend is designed so you can settle in and enjoy the borgo without needing to go anywhere else. Between events, there will be time to enjoy the pool, terraces, views, historic lanes, and gathering spaces around the property.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <h2>Getting Here and Having a Car</h2>
    <p>Laticastelli is tucked into the Tuscan countryside, but the weekend is designed so you can settle in and enjoy the borgo without needing to go anywhere else. Between events, there will be time to enjoy the pool, terraces, views, historic lanes, and gathering spaces around the property. You won’t need a car for the wedding weekend.</p>
    <p>Once you arrive at Laticastelli, everything is designed so you can settle in, slow down, and stay onsite. If you do choose to drive, complimentary parking is available at the borgo. And if you’re extending your time in Tuscany, a car can be a lovely way to reach the smaller hill towns, vineyards, and tucked-away places that are a little harder to discover by train.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section tight>
    <Figure ratio="3 / 2" label="Venue photo: terrace seating" />
    <Figure narrow ratio="2 / 3" label="Venue photo: balcony view" />
    <Figure ratio="3 / 2" label="Venue photo: cellar restaurant" />
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <h2>Navigating the Borgo</h2>
    <p>Laticastelli is a historic borgo with stone lanes, steps, and changes in level. If you have any mobility needs, please let us know so we can work with Ani to plan the most appropriate room and arrangements.</p>
  </Section>
</Base>
